        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Mortar is the connective matrix between masonry units. It transfers load, accommodates dimensional tolerance, seals against weather, and — critically — must be **softer and weaker than the unit it bonds**. When mortar is too hard, differential thermal movement cracks units instead of joints. The joint is the sacrificial element by design."
    },
